    "\n",
    "### Construction order in McStasScript\n",
    "\n",
    "Create the instrument object first, then register parameters, add components in beamline order, set each component's parameters, and finally set its placement and rotation. For example, `instr.add_component(\"guide\", \"Guide\", AT=[0, 0, 0.1], RELATIVE=\"source\")` creates an instance named `guide` of component type `Guide`. A string such as `\"guide_length\"` means “use this instrument parameter”; a number such as `2.0` is a literal value. Keep generated component names unique."
