    "## 4. Build 1: source, guide segment, and pulse-shaping chopper (PSC)\n",
    "\n",
    "The PSC teaching instrument is a compact line: source → 2 m guide → PSC. Put the source at the origin. The guide begins 0.1 m downstream and the PSC is 2.12 m from the source, leaving a 0.02 m clearance. Add wavelength or TOF monitors before and after the PSC; restoring monitors record and pass on the neutron.\n",
    "\n",
    "The neutron speed and flight time are\n",
    "\\[\n",
    "v=\\frac{C}{\\lambda},\\qquad t=\\frac{L\\lambda}{C},\\qquad\n",
    "C=3956.0346\\;\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}\\,\\AA}.\n",
    "\\]\n",
    "For a disk with opening \\(\\theta\\) degrees at frequency \\(\\nu\\), the open time is \\(w=\\theta/(360\\nu)\\). A useful source-time-centre estimate is \\(t_s=t_{pulse}/2+\\tau(n+1)/n\\). The centre arrival of a wavelength band is \\(t_c=t_s+L_c(\\lambda_{min}+\\lambda_{max})/(2C)\\), and its phase is \\(\\phi=\\mathrm{mod}(360\\nu t_c,360^\\circ)\\). These estimates should be checked against the before/after monitors.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Build sequence at a glance\n",
    "\n",
    "You will build and check five versions of the beamline:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Source, short guide and one PSC, to learn component syntax and chopper phase.\n",
    "2. Add guide 2 and a BC, then compare monitors around both choppers.\n",
    "3. Start a separate production instrument with the full elliptic primary guide and a 2–4 Å source band. This production model has no choppers.\n",
    "4. Add one analyser wedge and its two tubes; verify geometry before replication.\n",
    "5. Generate the full 30-channel analyser arc and 60 tube monitors with loops.\n",
    "\n",
    "The PSC and BC exercises teach timing concepts. They are not included in the final production beamline."
   ]
  },
