    "## 5. Build 2: add the bandwidth chopper (BC)\n",
    "\n",
    "Continue the teaching chopper line from the PSC. A 10 m second guide starts 0.02 m after the PSC; the BC centre is another 0.02 m after that guide. Thus \\(L_{PSC,BC}=10.04\\,\\mathrm{m}\\). With source-to-PSC distance 2.12 m, the source-to-BC flight path is 12.16 m.\n",
    "\n",
    "For a selected wavelength span \\(\\Delta\\lambda\\), estimate the BC gate requirement as\n",
    "\\[\n",
    "w_{req}=t_{pulse}+\\frac{L_{source,BC}\\Delta\\lambda}{C}.\n",
    "\\]\n",
    "For opening \\(\\theta_{BC}\\), source frequency \\(f_s\\), and integer harmonic \\(m\\), the BC rate is \\(\\nu_{BC}=m f_s\\) and its gate is \\(w_{BC}=\\theta_{BC}/(360\\nu_{BC})\\). Choose the largest integer harmonic whose gate is at least the required window. Centre the BC phase on the selected band arrival. This is a first estimate: confirm the selected band with wavelength and TOF monitors around the BC.\n",
    "\n",
    "Keep the distances explicit in the component tree. The 0.02 m gaps are part of the source-to-BC flight path, so include them in timing calculations. A placement such as `AT=[0, 0, 10.04], RELATIVE=\"PSC\"` is measured from the PSC origin along its local beam axis; it does not mean “10.04 m from the source.”"
