    "At zero offset this is 0°, 4°, …, 116° (30 channels, not 31). Each centre has its own analyser and detector pair. Before expanding, replace the one-channel rectangular focus with a full-bank angular focus aimed at the 60° bank midpoint: set `target_x=sin((offset+60)*M_PI/180.0)`, `target_y=0`, `target_z=cos((offset+60)*M_PI/180.0)`, `focus_aw=120`, and `focus_ah=4`.\n",
    "\n",
    "The code below is a starter pattern for the repeated components. Use it in a fresh production instrument after the primary line and sample are defined; do not run it on an object where `ana_arm0` and `monochromator0` already exist.\n",
    "\n",
    "The sample's focus must now illuminate the complete analyser arc rather than one analyser face. Its central direction is the 60° arc midpoint. The full horizontal and vertical openings are 120° and 4°. For the analyser positions, use\n",
    "\\[\n",
    "(x_k,y_k,z_k)=\\bigl(d_{sa}\\sin\\alpha_k,\\,0,\\,d_{sa}\\cos\\alpha_k\\bigr).\n",
    "\\]\n",
    "The repeated channels share the same wavelength, crystal spacing, blade layout, detector dimensions, and acquisition window; only their angular positions and output filenames differ."
